se header."],["2b9ce426_eac0fdfa",21,0,0,"mediumTimes are limited to 3 minutes. Is it enough?"],["92acd09a_3f2f9eee",21,0,1,"would it be interesting to know the number of completed providers too? (is it 10 out of 10 that expired or 10 out of 100?)"]],0,680],[7234793,20430,28,0.622,0.461,[[0,527]],[],0,681],[7216290,20431,268,6.361,5.1,[[7,0.882,107,233],[11,0.118,11,31]],[["309cbf88_11197efe",22,-6,1,"Is there a notion of successfully? IIUC, we just know that the task completed (as opposed to timed out). Should this be renamed IOS.BackgroundRefresh.StartupWait.Completed ?"],["3d97a3c8_bee107ed",21,-6,1,"IIUC, these two scenario seem very different. In one case, the task did not even start (the waiting timed out), and in the other case, the task itself timed out. Is it OK to log them together?"],["1cad735b_06fbfc32",19,-1,1,"optional: I would define veriable closer to where it is used, so I would revert the definitions of weakSelf and taskClosure, making moth task and weakSelf definition just before their usage."],["92e15aa1_dbcbc2ce",21,-1,0,"optional nit: we can have a base::optional<base::TimeDelta> for _startupWaitDuration to avoid the need for _hasStartupWaitDuration."],["a709694c_13fe1856",22,-1,1,"nit: typo? \"by\"?"],["e02ab699_ad128be0",19,-1,1,"nit: no need to test weakSelf"]],0,682]]}